/T (Figure 8 shows the top-15 Random Forest feature importances. APIs \(0.100\) and files_suspicious \(0.100\) are the leading discriminators, followed by files_text \(0.092\) and files_malicious \(0.081\). Registry features collectively account for approximately 20% of total importance. Notably, network features \(network_http: 0.052, network_connections: 0.052\) carry lower individual importance than file-based counters, suggesting that modern ransomware families have converged on more similar network profiles than file interaction patterns.)
