782 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The quality framework applied here has three principal limitations. First, the KS test and MMD-proxy treat features independently; joint distributional properties \(e.g., the correlation structure between registry_read and registry_total\) are not evaluated. A multivariate two-sample test \(e.g., Energy Distance or kernel MMD with an RBF kernel on the full feature vector\) would provide a more complete assessment. Second, the negative-value realism check is a necessary but not sufficient condition: a sample could have all non-negative values but represent a behaviorally impossible combination \(e.g., more registry deletes than registry reads\). Third, all evaluations are conducted against the training distribution; ground-truth evaluation against real unseen ransomware samples would require live telemetry validation beyond the scope of this study.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
