793 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Key Finding. No single generation strategy achieves high scores across all quality axes simultaneously, which validates the design decision to run all three in combination. CrossBreed provides the most realistic samples \(lowest KS, lowest MMD-proxy, fewest negative values\). CentroidPush provides the most diverse and geometrically novel samples. GaussianMorph provides the most extreme magnitude amplification. For production deployment, a recommended mix is: 40% CentroidPush + 35% CrossBreed + 25% GaussianMorph \(post-ReLU clipping\), balancing realism, diversity, and extremity in the augmentation pipeline.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
